name    snake
prog    snake
# h/j/k/l steer the snake, and it does respond -- the board is drawn and the
# snake moves. KEPT FAILING ON PURPOSE, 2026-08-28, for two reasons that are
# both real and neither is the harness's:
#   `orphans' -- 17 cursor moves arrive as literal `[13;49H' text and land
#   on the board where a person would see them. A fresh build from the
#   fixed source behaves identically, so the echo fix in SRC/snake/move.c
#   is not the cure; the comment there has the byte stream.
#   `expect moves' -- the game only says "You made N moves." when the snake
#   dies, and it does not die inside the time this script plays for. Left
#   in: the day snake can be driven to its end, this is what proves it.
wait    3
keys    llll
wait    1
keys    jjjj
wait    1
keys    hhhh
wait    1
keys    kkkk
wait    3
expect  moves
